  "description": "Build 415 default: the open-window survey. Rust engine, mean-degree window [0, 16] with the cap armed from N=1024, so rungs 64 and 256 run with no cap of any kind and the base block carries an unclamped prefix (how fast a law's density runs away) before any boundary applies. Campaign 1 of build 414 measured what the old [1.5, 8] window cost: 142 of 461 laws (30.8%) were pinned at the cap reading 8.03/8.01/8.00, only 8 of them ever produced a d_s value, and 199 more sat below the floor producing none, so 74% of the population was unreadable by construction. Filters armed from N=256, unfiltered fraction 0.25, extension ladder 65536 and 262144, three seeds on every rung, gsd-stability-score-8: two blocks of 50 (d_s and mean degree) with the branching-line, metric-class and control-family gates unchanged. Blind and uniform below the anchor; nothing is selected on the way up.",
